<section class="program-dossier__panel" id="program-panel-exocore" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="program-tab-exocore" hidden>
  <header class="program-dossier__masthead">
    <div><p class="research-eyebrow">Exocore / system ecology</p><h3>An ecology for agents, records, tools, governance, and creative practice.</h3></div>
    <p>Exocore is a systems research frame for understanding how people, memory, interfaces, and bounded tools can work together without turning a tool’s capability into authority.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="program-dossier__layout">
    <section><p class="research-eyebrow">Core question</p><strong>What makes a complex working environment legible, resumable, and corrigible?</strong><p>The answer is not a central mind. It is a set of relationships: human roles, source-bound memory, tool limits, visible gates, and a reliable way back.</p></section>
    <section><p class="research-eyebrow">System ecology</p><dl><div><dt>Harness</dt><dd>A bounded task room with named context, tools, stops, and return.</dd></div><div><dt>Continuity packet</dt><dd>State, sources, limits, and one responsible next decision.</dd></div><div><dt>Human return</dt><dd>The point where consequential judgment can be inspected or withheld.</dd></div></dl></section>
  </div>
  <section class="program-dossier__sequence" aria-label="Exocore study sequence"><div><span>01</span><strong>Orient</strong><p>Map people, records, tools, policies, and interfaces.</p></div><div><span>02</span><strong>Bound</strong><p>Set privacy, source, permission, and stop conditions.</p></div><div><span>03</span><strong>Attempt</strong><p>Use a tool for one local, inspectable transformation.</p></div><div><span>04</span><strong>Continue</strong><p>Return evidence, uncertainty, and control to a person.</p></div></section>
  <aside class="program-dossier__boundary"><strong>Public boundary</strong><p>Exocore is a research orientation, not a claim of a deployed autonomous platform. The public projection excludes private memory, credentials, and live operating state.</p></aside>
</section>
